From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Connor Buchan <mikey@blindcomputing.org>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 14:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: mc13892: use revision 2 VPLL voltage table

The MC13892 regulator driver has used the same VPLL table as VDIG since
its introduction.  That describes older silicon, but the Rev. 19 data
sheet specifies 1.20, 1.25, 1.50 and 1.80 V for the four VPLL selectors.
Freescale's vendor driver also treats selector 2 as 1.50 V starting with
revision 2.0 while retaining 1.65 V for older revisions.

Keep the existing table for pre-2.0 silicon and select the documented
VPLL table after identifying revision 2.0 or newer.  This only changes
the regulator framework's selector-to-voltage mapping; it does not write
the voltage selector during probe.

Upstream: Not submitted
Signed-off-by: Michael Connor Buchan <mikey@blindcomputing.org>
---
 drivers/regulator/mc13892-regulator.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/regulator/mc13892-regulator.c b/drivers/regulator/mc13892-regulator.c
--- a/drivers/regulator/mc13892-regulator.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/mc13892-regulator.c
@@ -18,6 +18,8 @@
 #include "mc13xxx.h"
 
 #define MC13892_REVISION			7
+#define MC13892_REVISION_REVFULL_M		(0x3 << 3)
+#define MC13892_REVISION_REVFULL_2_0		(0x2 << 3)
 
 #define MC13892_POWERCTL0			13
 #define MC13892_POWERCTL0_USEROFFSPI		3
@@ -192,6 +194,10 @@ static const unsigned int mc13892_vpll[] = {
 	1050000, 1250000, 1650000, 1800000,
 };
 
+static const unsigned int mc13892_vpll_rev2[] = {
+	1200000, 1250000, 1500000, 1800000,
+};
+
 static const unsigned int mc13892_vdig[] = {
 	1050000, 1250000, 1650000, 1800000,
 };
@@ -559,6 +565,12 @@ static int mc13892_regulator_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_unlock;
 
+	/* VPLL selector voltages changed in revision 2.0 silicon. */
+	if ((val & MC13892_REVISION_REVFULL_M) >=
+	    MC13892_REVISION_REVFULL_2_0)
+		mc13892_regulators[MC13892_VPLL].desc.volt_table =
+			mc13892_vpll_rev2;
+
 	/* enable switch auto mode (on 2.0A silicon only) */
 	if ((val & 0x0000FFFF) == 0x45d0) {
 		ret = mc13xxx_reg_rmw(mc13892, MC13892_SWITCHERS4,
-- 
2.51.0
